- Mental status: orientation to time/place/person, immediate recall (3 words), and attention (e.g., serial 7s or spelling “world” backward);  
- Cranial nerves II–VII: visual fields to confrontation, extraocular movements, facial symmetry at rest and with smiling/eyelid closure;  
- Motor: hand grip strength bilaterally, pronator drift with eyes closed.  
Report any asymmetry or abnormality.

